<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="csrf-token" content={get_csrf_token()} />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Eltrix is a Matrix homeserver written in Elixir. This site is generated from the project's own test status."
    />
    <.live_title default="Eltrix" suffix=" · Eltrix">{assigns[:page_title]}</.live_title>
    <link phx-track-static rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/css/app.css"} />
    <%!--
      Plausible, self-hosted, and only where a domain is configured — www sets
      it and beta does not, so staging traffic never lands in the production
      property.

      `data-domain` is the *apex*. Plausible matches it against the registered
      site exactly and discards anything else server-side, so a value of
      "www.eltrix.org" would load the script, return 202, and leave the
      dashboard empty forever with nothing anywhere reporting a fault.

      No cookies and no personal data, so no consent banner. The privacy policy
      was rewritten in the same commit that added this — a site that serves a
      document saying "no analytics" while running analytics is exactly the
      failure the rest of this codebase exists to prevent.
    --%>
    <script
      :if={@analytics_domain}
      defer
      data-domain={@analytics_domain}
      src="https://stats.oddie.app/js/script.js"
    >
    </script>
    <%!--
      No inline theme script.

      The generator ships one that reads localStorage and stamps data-theme
      before paint. It is dropped here for two reasons: this site has no theme
      toggle — it follows prefers-color-scheme and nothing else — and an inline
      script is exactly what the server's own CSP forbids, a rule that cost a
      round when the web client shipped its module inline. Nothing here needs
      JavaScript to render.
    --%>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

    <header class="masthead">
      <div class="wrap">
        <a class="brand" href={~p"/"}>eltrix</a>
        <%!--
          Primary navigation is what the project *is*. The terms, the privacy
          policy and the abuse path used to sit here, which made a product page
          read like a compliance page — they are obligations, published and
          reachable as §4.7 requires, and the footer is where obligations live.
        --%>
        <nav class="top" aria-label="Primary">
          <.link navigate={~p"/#features"}>What it does</.link>
          <.link navigate={~p"/#clients"}>Clients</.link>
          <.link navigate={~p"/#why"}>Why Elixir</.link>
          <.link navigate={~p"/status"}>Status</.link>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      {@inner_content}
    </main>

    <footer class="foot">
      <div class="wrap">
        <nav aria-label="Secondary">
          <.link navigate={~p"/status"}>Status</.link>
          <.link navigate={~p"/terms"}>Terms</.link>
          <.link navigate={~p"/privacy"}>Privacy</.link>
          <.link navigate={~p"/abuse"}>Report abuse</.link>
          <.link navigate={~p"/imprint"}>Imprint</.link>
        </nav>
        <p>
          Eltrix is a Matrix homeserver written in Elixir. The capability
          statuses on this site are generated from the project's own criteria,
          and the build fails if a page claims more than they say.
        </p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
